---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CopyBlock from '../components/CopyBlock.astro';
import { getGroups, projectInstructions, version } from '../lib/rpm.mjs';
const groups = getGroups();
---
<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Sandminni · PPM · PPMP v{version}</p>
      <h1>Durable project memory,<br />grain by grain.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Sandminni is the public product brand for Persistent Project Memory (PPM), the first reference Skill implementation of PPMP. PPMP defines portable project-memory semantics; Sandminni turns them into an operational workflow.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/quick-start">Get started</a><a class="button secondary" href="/reference">Read the reference</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="terminal-card" aria-label="Sandminni and PPMP architecture"><div class="terminal-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><pre><code>PPMP protocol
      ↓
Sandminni
PPM Skill
      ↓
repository backend
+ ChatGPT adapter</code></pre></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell" id="copy-setup">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 · Reference setup</p><h2>Set up Sandminni.</h2></div><p>The PPM reference stack preserves the simple repository-backed workflow while keeping repository and ChatGPT mechanics outside PPMP itself.</p></div>
    <CopyBlock value={projectInstructions} title="PPM Project Instructions" language="markdown" label="Copy instructions" />
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Architecture</p><h2>Semantics separated from mechanics.</h2></div>
    <div class="principle-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Protocol</h3><p>PPMP defines current state, next steps, decisions, checkpoints, classification, persistence semantics, and compatibility.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Implementation</h3><p>Sandminni is the public brand for Persistent Project Memory (PPM), which turns PPMP semantics into operational Skill behavior without redefining the protocol.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Backend + adapter</h3><p>Storage and platform integration are replaceable. Repository/Git and ChatGPT are the initial reference choices, not PPMP requirements.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 · Reference</p><h2>Repository-owned specification.</h2></div><p>The site renders canonical files directly at build time. RPM v1 remains preserved in Git history as the predecessor design.</p></div>
    <div class="reference-grid">{groups.map((group) => (<article class="reference-card"><p class="eyebrow">{group.label}</p><p>{group.description}</p><ul>{group.documents.slice(0, 7).map((doc) => (<li><a href={`/${doc.kind}/${doc.slug}`}>{doc.title}<span>→</span></a></li>))}</ul></article>))}</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
